    background: "Wallace Clement Sabine was asked to fix the poor acoustics of the Fogg Art Museum at Harvard in the 1890s. By comparing rooms of known volume and varying the amount of padded seating, he discovered that reverberation time depends mainly on the ratio of volume to total sound absorption. His rule T₆₀ = 0.161 V / A remains the first quantitative design formula in architectural acoustics, valid when the sound field is sufficiently diffuse.",
