      "4. Estimate the triangle's area by measuring its side lengths and using the spherical excess relation, or by imaging and pixel counting.",
      "5. Repeat for triangles of different sizes and on different parts of the sphere to test whether the angle excess scales with area.",
      "6. Repeat on the cylinder and cone, confirming zero excess for triangles that avoid the cone apex.",
      "7. Use a computer algebra system to compute the curvature from the metric of each surface and compare with the measured values.",
